  "question": {
    "html": "<p>When small particles with charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> are dropped between two horizontal plates in vacuum near the surface of the Earth, they fall downwards with constant velocity. The electric field strength between the plates is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E\"></span>. What is true about the mass of the particles?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"mass = \\frac{EQ}{g}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"mass &gt; \\frac{EQ}{g}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"mass &lt; \\frac{EQ}{g}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">The mass of the particles is negligible.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
